"""Append non-destructive Stage1044 NE-anchor/dual-transmitter sensitivity to latest
single-cell page, preserving existing, MORE ADVANCED Stage1018/1043 analyses.
No numerical force-fit to different-modality scRNAseq.
"""
from pathlib import Path
S=Path(r'G:\Spatial_gene_site_publish\perilc-map6-review\single-cell.html')
data=S.read_text(encoding='utf8')
if 'id="stage1044-ne-calibration"' in data:
 print('STAGE1044_ALREADY_PRESENT')
 raise SystemExit(0)
page='''<section id="stage1044-ne-calibration">
<h2>Stage1044 — LC-NE reference sensitivity, corrected marker gates, and unresolved VGAT/VGLUT2 co-detection</h2>
<p class="lead"><b>Do not force NE transmitter colocalization to zero.</b> We used the current all-71,950-cell RouteA 27-gene count matrix, fixed previous Fine26/NE01 source labels, and independent existing scRNA NE cluster. An initial overly permissive Slc6a2&gt;5 exclusion misidentified 11,892 Snap25&gt;5 cells as NE candidates, but only 15.0% belonged to the frozen NE01 cluster. Slc6a2&gt;200 instead identifies 1,715 cells with 97.6% NE01 concordance and 93.5% recall of the frozen NE01 class. This is <em>agreement with a partially gene-derived FISH classification</em>, NOT an independent true-NE specificity score.</p>
<div class="cards">
<article class="card"><h3>NE marker threshold sensitivity: why Slc6a2&gt;5 excluded too many neurons</h3><a href="assets/stage998_ne_reference_threshold/STAGE998b_NE_ANCHOR_SENSITIVITY.png"><img loading="lazy" src="assets/stage998_ne_reference_threshold/STAGE998b_NE_ANCHOR_SENSITIVITY.png" alt="NE anchor threshold sensitivity and VGAT VGLUT2 dual calls"></a><p>Using Snap25&gt;5, excluding NE01 or Slc6a2&gt;200, plus ChAT01 or Slc5a7&gt;50 leaves 47,454 eligible cells BEFORE VGAT/VGLUT2 OR gating. At VGAT&gt;15/VGLUT2&gt;5, there are 8,598 double-positive among eligible cells (18.12%) but 31.48% double-positive among either-transmitter-positive cells. The latter is the comparable denominator to the previously published Stage1043 strict-positive gate. <a href="data/stage998b_ne_anchor_selection_robustness.csv">All anchor choices and 6 threshold pairs</a>.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Actual independent scRNA NE n=36 cannot define an exact FISH spot cutoff</h3><a href="assets/stage998_ne_reference_threshold/STAGE998c_NE_SCSEQ36_REFERENCE_CAVEAT.png"><img loading="lazy" src="assets/stage998_ne_reference_threshold/STAGE998c_NE_SCSEQ36_REFERENCE_CAVEAT.png" alt="NE scRNA36 comparison and uncertainty interval"></a><p>Existing periLC single-cell cluster NE n=36 detects VGAT and VGLUT2 in 1/36 (2.78%) each, Wilson 95% CI ~0.49–14.17%. These are RNA-seq UMI dropouts, not per-cell FISH spot ground truth. The thresholds that <em>would mechanically match</em> 2.78% NE positivity are about VGAT 52.1 and VGLUT2 29.4 corrected counts, but applying them would force away many other cells and is not scientifically justified. The larger published Stage1015 own 4,701 neuron raw UMI comparison (1.55% dual), and Stage1016 Allen Pons 143,661 cells (1.28% raw UMI dual) are higher-priority broad references but do not specify an LC FISH cutoff.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Full-section spatial double-marker patterns after stricter NE source exclusion</h3><a href="assets/stage999_transmitter_spatial_strictNE/STAGE999_FULL_SECTION_GABA_GLU_COLOCALIZATION_VGAT15_VGLUT5.png"><img loading="lazy" src="assets/stage999_transmitter_spatial_strictNE/STAGE999_FULL_SECTION_GABA_GLU_COLOCALIZATION_VGAT15_VGLUT5.png" alt="Whole S500 S530 S560 XY double-positive after stricter NE and ChAT exclusion"></a><p>S500 3,389/23,246 eligible double-positive; S530 2,559/13,365; S560 2,650/10,843. Tissue-boundary enrichment is inconsistent by section. No presumptive grid phase or raw spot data are changed. This is a reference-gate sensitivity plot, not a replacement for Stage1018 actual 25-tile overlap geometry or Stage1043 exact user gating.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Remaining dual-positive dependence on threshold and tissue boundary</h3><a href="assets/stage999_transmitter_spatial_strictNE/STAGE999_DOUBLE_POSITIVE_TISSUE_EDGE_ENRICHMENT.png"><img loading="lazy" src="assets/stage999_transmitter_spatial_strictNE/STAGE999_DOUBLE_POSITIVE_TISSUE_EDGE_ENRICHMENT.png"></a><p>For VGAT&gt;15 and VGLUT2&gt;5, near-edge/deep-tissue double-positive ratios are S500 0.82, S530 1.27, S560 0.69. This has no consistent tissue-edge direction; the larger prior Stage1018 physical-tile analysis should remain the actual seam authority. <a href="data/stage999_double_positive_true_tissue_edge_screen_STRICT_NE.csv">All section and threshold counts</a>.</p></article>
</div>
<p class="lead"><b>Decision:</b> report VGAT-only, VGLUT2-only, both, neither, NE and cholinergic reference populations separately. Low-expressing Snap25-positive unassigned cells should remain visible as an uncertainty category, not be relabeled non-neurons. Do NOT optimize VGAT/VGLUT2 to match 1–2% whole-brain RNA-seq coexpression: measurement modality, sample depth and LC/periLC anatomy differ. The LC-NE gene-expression continuum in <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-026-11026-0">Su et al., Nature 2026</a>, the periLC GABA populations in <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-025-08952-w">Luskin et al., Nature 2025</a> and <a href="https://alleninstitute.github.io/abc_atlas_access/notebooks/10x_snRNASeq_tutorial_part_2b.html">Allen neurotransmitter examples</a> motivate separate gene-reference validation, not artificial suppression of Slc17a6 in NE cells. <a href="data/stage998c_independent_NE_scRNA36_vs_Map10_FISH_threshold_QC.csv">Exact cross-modal comparison</a>.</p>
</section>'''
tag='<section id="stage1043-user-strict-gate">'
assert tag in data
data=data.replace(tag,page+tag,1)
nav='<nav><a href="index.html">'
if nav in data:
 data=data.replace(nav,'<nav><a href="#stage1044-ne-calibration">New: NE anchor / dual-GABA-Glu QC</a><a href="index.html">',1)
S.write_text(data,encoding='utf8')
print('STAGE1044_SITE_SECTION_ADDED',len(page),len(data))
